## Likely follow-up questions

**Q: Where is the +1?**

Only on "end": the function ran through the whole of tick t. After it, the next free tick is t + 1.

**Q: Complexity?**

O(L) time, O(depth) stack.

**Q: A multi-threaded program.**

One stack per thread id in the log; the CPU-ownership rule then applies per thread.

**Q: Millions of log lines from a live service.**

Stream them; keep only the stacks and totals. This is what a profiler's self-time column is.

**Q: Related?**

InterviewDB Q6 (matched parentheses) — the same stack discipline; Q7 (scheduled executor) for the time side.

